invariant: INV-14
file: srv_resume.c
catches: srv_flight_test
reason: the lifetime check admits a ticket one second past SRV_TICKET_LIFETIME,
  so a server issues tickets whose ticket_lifetime understates how long it
  honours them, and a build at the RFC 9846 §4.7.1 cap of 604800 seconds
  accepts a ticket older than the seven days the section allows
  (rfc9846.txt:3257-3261). test/srv_resume_tests.h resumes at the last
  valid second and requires the next one to be passed over.

--- old
    return now_seconds >= auth_seconds && now_seconds - auth_seconds <= SRV_TICKET_LIFETIME;
--- new
    return now_seconds >= auth_seconds && now_seconds - auth_seconds <= SRV_TICKET_LIFETIME + 1;
